op6: SweetGPUUserClient msm DRM uAPI subset + BO/IB submit (GPU milestone G2)

When sweetgpu=2 leaves the Adreno 630 running after G1, bsd/dev/sweet_gpu.c
initializes a 4K-page bitmap allocator over the remaining GPU carve-out
(16K-aligned for XNU's 16K VM device pager, mapped with 4K PTEs into the
GPU SMMU at 0x10000000 + p*4K with 64 page-table pages and CB_TLBIALL/
CB_TLBSYNC invalidation), wraps the 32 KiB ringbuffer, and exposes C entry
points for parameter queries, BO allocation/free, CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER +
CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE + CP_EVENT_WRITE(CACHE_FLUSH_TS) submission, and fence
completion polling.

iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetGPU.cpp publishes SweetGPU numeric properties as
64-bit OSNumbers (fixing ioreg's sign-extension of 0xC0FFEE01), sets
IOUserClientClass = "SweetGPUUserClient", and implements the Linux msm DRM
uAPI subset over IOUserClient (selectors 0x09 GEM_CLOSE, 0x40 GET_PARAM,
0x41 SET_PARAM, 0x42 GEM_NEW, 0x43 GEM_INFO, 0x44 GEM_CPU_PREP,
0x45 GEM_CPU_FINI, 0x46 GEM_SUBMIT, 0x47 WAIT_FENCE, 0x48 GEM_MADVISE,
0x4a..0x4c SUBMITQUEUE_*, plus clientMemoryForType returning a write-combine
physical IOMemoryDescriptor for IOConnectMapMemory64).

Origin: ios-op6 project code (MIT), with uAPI dispatch and ring submission
patterns referencing oosexgang/hackios-xnu-kernel @ 63fc2b4
(drivers/gpu/hakios.adreno.c and drivers/gpu/hakios.gpu.cpp, APSL 2.0) and
Mesa's drm-uapi/msm_drm.h (MIT). No Linux or Bergamota code.
Applies on top of 0107 (xnu-8796.141.3 + 0000-0107).

